  "name": "Question 12",
  "problem": "If the set $U$ containing all integers is the universal set and $X={0,-1,-2,-3,-4,\u2026}$, then $\\overset{\u2015}{X}=$",
  "worked_solution": "The complement of $X,$ denoted $\\overset{\u2015}{X},$ consists of every element in the universal set $U$ that is not in the set $X.$\n\nThe universal set $U$ consists of the integer numbers while the set $X$ consists of the negative integers and $0.$\n\nSo, the only elements of $U$ that are not in $X$ are the natural numbers.\n\nTherefore, the complement of $X$ is\n\n$$\n\\overset{\u2015}{X}={1,2,3,\u2026}.\n$$",
